<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!-- Linear-side drain for parked, auto-filed issues (BRO-293, BRO-286
         Phase 2 completion). Ticks 3x/day (10:30/14:30/18:30 ET — offset
         30min from backlog-drain.plist's 10/14/18 so the two never spawn
         detached children in the same worktree-lock window) and runs
         scripts/linear-drain-parked.js, which dispatches up to 3 parked
         issues owner-alert-router.js auto-filed through linear-next.js's
         own --headless path (full guard stack: kill switch, idempotency,
         terminal-state, dead-dispatch, verify gate).

         Not wired into data-health-check.yml: the CI runner has no `claude`
         binary to hand a dispatched job to, so this has to run somewhere
         with one — this Mac, same as backlog-drain.js's own launchd tick.

         INSTALLED AND RUNNING since 2026-09-08 (BRO-3060). Do NOT read
         this file to learn whether the agent is live — a copy of it sits in
         ~/Library/LaunchAgents/ and can drift from this one. Check the
         running system instead:
           launchctl print gui/$(id -u)/com.broadwayscore.linear-drain-parked \
             | grep -E "runs =|last exit code"
         For 26 days before this was bootstrapped, 126 auto-filed issues
         (median age 19 days) sat parked with a do-not-dispatch sentinel and
         NO ledger row of any kind, because this drain — the thing built to
         release them — had never executed once. The supervised runs this
         file's old header asked for have happened and are on the record:
         a --dry-run shakedown (3 candidates, attempt-memory reconciled
         BRO-334/BRO-335 to card-pass off their job-done rows), then a live
         `launchctl kickstart -k` tick that produced 3/3 dispatch attempts
         and a `launch` + `job-spawned` pair for BRO-346 in
         data/audit/dispatch-ledger.jsonl.

         To turn it OFF without deleting anything (the kill switch is
         preferred — it stops dispatch while leaving the tick and its logs
         in place, so a dead drain still looks different from a disabled
         one): set LINEAR_NEXT_DISABLED=1 in .env. To stop future ticks
         entirely, `launchctl bootout` per the note below.

         StartCalendarInterval entries are LOCAL TIME on this Mac
         (America/New_York, DST-safe — launchd reads the system clock).

         Secrets (LINEAR_API_KEY) come from the repo's .env via
         load-env.js's own chain — launchd does NOT inherit shell env; no
         secrets are read directly by this plist.

         Install (owner action, after reviewing a manual run's output):
           cp scripts/launchd/com.broadwayscore.linear-drain-parked.plist ~/Library/LaunchAgents/
           launchctl bootstrap gui/$(id -u) ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.broadwayscore.linear-drain-parked.plist
         Manual run (no launchd): node scripts/linear-drain-parked.js
         Manual tick via launchd: launchctl kickstart -k gui/$(id -u)/com.broadwayscore.linear-drain-parked
         Kill (stops FUTURE ticks only):
           launchctl bootout gui/$(id -u)/com.broadwayscore.linear-drain-parked

         Rollback story (mirrors backlog-drain.plist's own note): bootout
         does not touch an ALREADY-dispatched headless job — the spawn is
         detached and this script returns immediately once spawn() is
         called. To find/stop a live drain-dispatched job:
           cat data/audit/job-leases/*/lease.json   # {jobId, pid, cwd} per live task
           kill <pid>
         Per-attempt stdout/stderr for debugging a refused/failed dispatch:
           data/audit/digest-autofix-logs/linear_<identifier>-<ts>.log
           (dispatchDetached()'s own log dir — this drain reuses it, no
           separate log dir of its own)
         This drain's own attempt journal (which parked issues it has tried
         and when, for the retry-cooldown dedupe):
           data/audit/linear-drain-parked-ledger.jsonl -->
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>com.broadwayscore.linear-drain-parked</string>
    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>/bin/bash</string>
        <string>-c</string>
        <string>cd /Users/tompryor/Broadwayscore &amp;&amp; SYNC_TAG=linear-drain-parked bash scripts/lib/sync-audit-checkout.sh &amp;&amp; exec node scripts/linear-drain-parked.js</string>
    </array>
    <key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
    <array>
        <dict>
            <key>Hour</key>
            <integer>10</integer>
            <key>Minute</key>
            <integer>30</integer>
        </dict>
        <dict>
            <key>Hour</key>
            <integer>14</integer>
            <key>Minute</key>
            <integer>30</integer>
        </dict>
        <dict>
            <key>Hour</key>
            <integer>18</integer>
            <key>Minute</key>
            <integer>30</integer>
        </dict>
    </array>
    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>/tmp/linear-drain-parked-launchd.log</string>
    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>/tmp/linear-drain-parked-launchd.log</string>
    <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
    <dict>
        <key>PATH</key>
        <string>/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:/Users/tompryor/.local/bin</string>
    </dict>
</dict>
</plist>
